| Prepare for Vanilla Conquer: Tiberian Dawn and Red Alert
| Installs the game data from the freeware CD images in the same directory as this
| file: the C&C95 (C&C Gold) GDI and Nod discs into !VanillaTD, and the Red Alert
| Allied and Soviet discs into !VanillaRA. Copy it next to the .iso files and
| double-click it, or from the command line:
|   *Obey <path>.Prepare [<CD image>...] [-nomovies] [-force]
| -nomovies leaves out the movies (about 430 MB per C&C95 disc, 370-415 MB per
| Red Alert disc).
| -force rewrites files that are already present.
If "<VanillaTD$Dir>"="" AND "<VanillaRA$Dir>"="" Then Error Prepare doesn't know where !VanillaTD or !VanillaRA is yet. Open the directory containing them, then run Prepare again.
Set Prepare$Dir <VanillaTD$Dir>
If "<Prepare$Dir>"="" Then Set Prepare$Dir <VanillaRA$Dir>
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 RMLoad <Prepare$Dir>.Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error Prepare needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later
| vcprep runs Utils.ramix in this slot too, to install Red Alert without its movies.
WimpSlot -min 6000K -max 6000K
| vcprep can't read the $Dir variables itself (UnixLib's getenv doesn't see them), so
| Prepare passes the application directories the Filer has seen.
Set Prepare$Apps ""
If "<VanillaTD$Dir>"<>"" Then Set Prepare$Apps -app <VanillaTD$Dir>
If "<VanillaRA$Dir>"<>"" Then Set Prepare$Apps <Prepare$Apps> -raapp <VanillaRA$Dir>
Run <Prepare$Dir>.Utils.vcprep <Prepare$Apps> -search <Obey$Dir> %*0
